# What must not reach a build context.
#
# `node_modules` above all: `deploy/Dockerfile` runs `pnpm install --prod`
# inside the image and then `COPY packages/ packages/`, so a host tree left in
# the context is copied over an install that has already happened — with this
# machine's symlinks and this machine's dev dependencies in it.
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules

# `deploy/` is deliberately NOT ignored: the image copies
# `deploy/healthcheck.mjs`, which is what its own HEALTHCHECK runs. Ignoring the
# directory would put the "Cannot find module" back.

# The suites and their corpus. `COPY packages/ packages/` is wholesale, so
# without these the image ships every `*.test.ts`, every `__tests__/` and the
# whole frozen fixture corpus into a production container that could never run
# any of it: `vitest` is a dev dependency and the install is `--prod`. Nothing
# under `src/` imports them — the fixture corpus is named in comments and in
# test files only — so this removes files rather than behaviour, and an image
# whose contents are only what runs is an image somebody can account for.
**/__tests__/
**/__fixtures__/
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.mjs
**/vitest.config.ts
**/vitest.setup.ts
